---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Security & Privacy — Vericore" description="Current Vericore 0.7.0 security, privacy, trust boundaries, and transparency information.">
  <section class="hero container"><span class="kicker">TRUST / TRANSPARENCY</span><h1>Know what Vericore<br /><span>does with your data.</span></h1><p>This page describes the current 0.7.0 implementation. It is intentionally limited to behavior that exists today.</p></section>
  <section class="container grid">
    <article><span class="kicker">LOCAL-FIRST</span><h2>Repository analysis</h2><p>Vericore analyzes repositories locally. With AI disabled, deterministic repository analysis does not send repository content to a Vericore telemetry or storage service.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">AI / OPT-IN</span><h2>Provider boundaries</h2><p>AI-assisted workflows are optional. When configured, bounded repository-derived context is sent directly to the selected provider for the requested operation. AI is not authoritative repository truth.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">REPORTS</span><h2>Self-contained output</h2><p>Generated HTML reports contain their visualization code and do not require a browser CDN request at report-open time, allowing offline inspection.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">API BOUNDARY</span><h2>Trusted local use</h2><p>The local REST server validates paths and applies rate limiting, but it does not provide authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, or deployment-level TLS. Do not expose it publicly without an appropriate security boundary.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">PATH SAFETY</span><h2>Bounded repositories</h2><p>Local server and MCP boundaries reject remote repository URLs and validate repository paths. Keep allowed roots as narrow as practical when configuring trusted integrations.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">CONTEXT LIMITS</span><h2>Bounded AI input</h2><p>AI operations use bounded repository-derived context rather than indiscriminately sending an entire repository. Exact limits and provider behavior are documented in the source repository.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">CHANGE SAFETY</span><h2>Verification is not authorization</h2><p>The Agent Change Contract is a deterministic verification boundary. It detects mismatches, tampering, stale state, and repository identity changes; it is not an authorization system or autonomous coding mechanism.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">LIMITATIONS</span><h2>What is not shipped</h2><p>There is no production telemetry service, multi-tenant governance layer, autonomous source modification, or deployment-grade authentication in the current release.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section class="container links"><a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore/blob/main/docs/DATA_PRIVACY.md">Read the detailed transparency document ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Read the security policy ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/Vericore/issues">Report an issue ↗</a></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.hero{padding:110px 0 65px;max-width:960px}.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em}.hero h1{margin:18px 0;font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.065em}.hero h1 span{color:var(--muted)}.hero p{max-width:700px;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.1rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:12px}.grid article{min-height:190px;padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--panel)}.grid h2{margin:15px 0 8px;font-size:1.3rem}.grid p{color:var(--muted)}.links{margin-top:70px;display:grid;gap:8px}.links a{padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;text-decoration:none;background:var(--panel)}.links a:hover{border-color:#304155}@media(max-width:700px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
